                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3569: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-11T14:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 11—11:41
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>391. My 388, November 10, 1 p.m.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d300-f1"/> Proposed loan
                    for administrative purposes would merely postpone public acknowledgment
                    governmental insolvency. Signs of collapse forecast, my 367, Oct. 22, 4 p.m.,
                    increase. Chinese newspapers anxiously discussing financial situation and
                    bankers manifesting uneasiness. Peking judges threaten strike, also clerks in
                    Government departments if salaries in arrears some months not paid. Ministers
                    War, Navy, Justice, handed in resignations; Premier desires to quit. Desperate
                    efforts will be made to stave off climax till after close of Washington
                    Conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
